To build this code, run the following:

aclocal
automake --add-missing
autoconf
./configure --prefix=/install-dir
make install

Then NRS.converter is installed in /install-dir/bin/

Options available from 'NRS.converter -h'

	case 's': // Timestep (in data samples)
	case 'l': // collapse to [0,1]
	case 'b': // first timetick to translate (in ms)
	case 'e': // final timetick to translate (in ms)
	case 'd': // differentiate neural signal (decay rate perhaps 0.9)
	case 'i': // averaging interval for normalisation (perhaps 50000)
	case 'f': // Find spikes in neuron
	case 't': // amount of recovery time for first spike on sound
	case 'r': // round sound to 0, 1
	case 'n': // Name of neuron if not Neuron*


NRS.converter Aff9c.dat data
NRS.converter -l -n Intra2 -d 0.9 -i 50000 Aff9c.dat data
NRS.converter -l -n Intra2 -d 0.9 -i 50000 -f 0.1 Aff9c.dat data